IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Crimes (Overseas) Act 1964 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL
-- GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1964A00116.txt (compilation of 3
-- October 2014). The Australian abroad asks: "Does this Act apply to what I
-- did overseas, so that Jervis Bay criminal law applies to me; what must
-- happen before I am prosecuted; by when must I be given a certificate, and
-- notify the prosecutor?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 3 Australian.
DECLARE `Status` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `a non-citizen permitted to remain in Australia indefinitely`
    `neither`

-- s 3A(1), (3)-(6): why I am there, and why I am not subject to local
-- prosecution.
DECLARE `Ground` IS ONE OF
    `diplomatic, consular or international-organisation immunity`
    `immune under a relevant agreement or arrangement while working under one`
    `working under a declared agreement or arrangement`
    `working for the Commonwealth in a declared foreign country or part`
    `none`

DECLARE `Overseas case` HAS
    `my status when I acted`                                        IS A `Status`
    `the ground`                                                    IS A `Ground`
    -- ss 3A(4)(d), (5)(d), (6)(d)
    `I am within any category the regulations specify`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3A(2)
    `I am or will become subject to local prosecution, which an Australian verdict would not end` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3A(10)
    `I was a Defence Force member when I acted`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was ASIS, AGO or ASD staff acting properly in its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(1)(b)
    `the act would breach Jervis Bay criminal law`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4(2)
    `the Minister has consented in writing`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(6), (8)(a)
    `the day the certificate is to be tendered`                     IS A DATE
    `the day of the hearing at which I want the issuer called`      IS A DATE

DECLARE `Overseas position` HAS
    `this Act applies to me for the act`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `Jervis Bay criminal law applies to my act`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `proceedings may be commenced`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I may be arrested or charged before consent`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day to give me a copy of a certificate`               IS A DATE
    `the last day to notify the prosecutor to call the issuer`      IS A DATE

§ `Rules`

@ref s 3 Australian
GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am an Australian` c IF
    NOT (c's `my status when I acted` EQUALS `neither`)

-- s 3A(1)-(6), (10).
@ref s 3A
GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies` c IF
        `I am an Australian` c
    AND NOT (c's `I was a Defence Force member when I acted`)
    AND NOT (c's `I was ASIS, AGO or ASD staff acting properly in its functions`)
    AND `a ground is met` c

GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground is met` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `the ground`
    -- s 3A(1)-(2): while the immunity holds
    WHEN `diplomatic, consular or international-organisation immunity` THEN
        NOT (c's `I am or will become subject to local prosecution, which an Australian verdict would not end`)
    -- s 3A(3)
    WHEN `immune under a relevant agreement or arrangement while working under one` THEN TRUE
    -- s 3A(4)-(6)
    WHEN `working under a declared agreement or arrangement` THEN c's `I am within any category the regulations specify`
    WHEN `working for the Commonwealth in a declared foreign country or part` THEN c's `I am within any category the regulations specify`
    WHEN `none` THEN FALSE

-- s 4(1): Jervis Bay Territory criminal law applies as Commonwealth law.
@ref s 4(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Jervis Bay law applies` c IF
        `the Act applies` c
    AND c's `the act would breach Jervis Bay criminal law`

-- s 4(2), (4): proceedings need the Minister's written consent; arrest,
-- charge, remand and bail do not.
@ref s 4(2), (4)
GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings may be commenced` c IF
        `Jervis Bay law applies` c
    AND c's `the Minister has consented in writing`

-- s 8(6): a copy of the certificate at least 14 days before it is tendered;
-- s 8(8)(a): at least 4 days' notice to call the issuer.
@ref s 8(6), (8)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last certificate day for` c MEANS c's `the day the certificate is to be tendered` MINUS 14

GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last notice day for` c MEANS c's `the day of the hearing at which I want the issuer called` MINUS 4

@ref ss 3, 3A, 4, 8
@export default The position of an Australian (a citizen or a non-citizen permitted to remain indefinitely) who did something in a foreign country, under the Crimes (Overseas) Act 1964 (Cth): whether the Act applies to them for the act (diplomatic, consular or international-organisation immunity while it holds; immunity under, or work under a declared, relevant agreement or arrangement; Commonwealth work in a declared country; not Defence Force members or intelligence staff acting properly: s 3A); whether the criminal law of the Jervis Bay Territory then applies to the act as Commonwealth law (s 4(1)); whether proceedings may be commenced (only with the Minister's written consent, though arrest and charge may come first: s 4(2), (4)); and the last days for the prosecution to give a copy of a certificate (14 days before) and for the accused to notify the prosecutor to call its issuer (4 days before: s 8). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Overseas case`  @desc My status, the ground for the Act's reach, any regulations' category, local prosecution, Defence or intelligence status, the act, the Minister's consent, and the hearing days
GIVETH A `Overseas position`
`the overseas position for` c MEANS
    `Overseas position` OF `the Act applies` c, `Jervis Bay law applies` c, `proceedings may be commenced` c,
                           `Jervis Bay law applies` c, `the last certificate day for` c, `the last notice day for` c
